<section class="py-12 bg-gray-50">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-center mb-2">THE NEUKWI NËU & SILVER JUBILEE</h1>
    <h2 class="text-xl text-center text-gray-600 mb-2">Fo’o NGWADEZA III & THE SILVER JUBILEE CELEBRATION OF HIS ENTHRONEMENT AS THE FON OF NSONGWA VILLAGE</h2>
    <p class="text-center text-amber-800 font-semibold mb-8">Theme: STEWARDSHIP & VISION [OFFICIAL PROGRAM]</p>
    
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Friday December 4th — Mametah (Day 0)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Village Cleansing</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li>The entire village will drop Atetoh at the palace square. After 7 days, it will be used for village purification. Kwihfo in all night communication with the Ancestors.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Saturday December 12th — Mametah (Day 1)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Opening & Cultural Cleansing (The Awakening)</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>6:00 AM:</strong> Campfire in replacement of gunshots across the seven hills of Nsongwa announcing the dawn of the jubilee.</li>
          <li><strong>7:00 AM:</strong> Sacred cleansing and purification rites by the Fon and Kwihfo at the palace shrines (Tap Tap).</li>
          <li><strong>8:00 AM:</strong> Arrival of the population. Arrival and Installation of Dignitaries:
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside ml-6 mt-1 space-y-1">
              <li>8:10 AM - Arrival of Religious, traditional authorities and leaders of legalized political parties</li>
              <li>8:20 AM - Arrival of Regional Delegate of RDAC and others</li>
              <li>8:30 AM - Arrival of Administrative and Municipal Authorities of Bamenda</li>
              <li>8:40 AM - Arrival of the Hon. President of the Administrative Court, the learned Attorney General and Hon. President of the court of Appeal</li>
              <li>8:50 AM - Arrival of the Honorable members of Parliament</li>
              <li>9:00 AM - Arrival of the City Mayor to the Bamenda City Council</li>
              <li>9:30 AM - Arrival of the Senior Divisional Officer for Mezam</li>
              <li>9:35 AM - Arrival of the Brigadier General, Commander for Bamenda accompanied by COM RG-5 and COM 51e BRIM</li>
              <li>9:40 AM - Arrival of the Vice Chancellor of the University of Bamenda</li>
              <li>9:45 AM - Arrival of the Public Independent Conciliator for the North West Region.</li>
              <li>9:50 AM - Arrival of the President of North West Region Assembly delegation</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li><strong>END OF ARRIVALS</strong></li>
          <li><strong>10:00 AM:</strong> Arrival of the Governor of the North West Region/ Minister of Arts and Culture/ MINAT</li>
          <li><strong>11:00 AM:</strong> Royal Procession led by the royal dance (Lerère)
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside ml-6 mt-1 space-y-1">
              <li>Singing of the National Anthem</li>
              <li>Singing of the Nsongwa Anthem</li>
              <li>Ecumenical Prayer</li>
              <li>A word of welcome by Prince Nathan Asanji (a crown prince after Coronation).</li>
              <li>Cutting of the Silver Jubilee Cake</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li><strong>SPEECHES:</strong>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside ml-6 mt-1 space-y-1">
              <li>Welcome Speech by the Nsongwa Traditional Council Chairman (NTC)</li>
              <li>Speech by HRM Fo’o Ngwadeza III</li>
              <li>Speech by the President of the House of Chiefs</li>
              <li>Speech by the Minister of Arts and Culture or the Governor of NWR</li>
              <li>Awards</li>
              <li>Twin Dance and Fumben Dance.</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li><strong>3:00 PM:</strong> MAGAZINE/MUSEUM LAUNCH by the Mayor of BCC / Mayor of Bamenda II</li>
          <li>Musical Entertainment by some Cameroonian Artists</li>
          <li><strong>06:00 PM:</strong> End of official Opening, Feasting and Entertainments. Traditional campfire lighting and evening storytelling sessions (Njallah) with village elders.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Sunday December 13th — Yidzong (Day 3)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Ecumenical Day (Prayers for Peace & Unity)</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>09:00 AM:</strong> Joint inter denominational prayers - Christians and Muslims alike. Ecumenical service for the health of HRM Fo’o Ngwadeza III & the safety of the village.</li>
          <li><strong>12:00 PM:</strong> Choral music competition featuring local, regional, and church choirs.</li>
          <li><strong>03:00 PM:</strong> Royal charity visit: Thanksgiving and food supplies for underprivileged and displaced Families within the subdivision.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Monday December 14th — Yakab (Day 4)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Education & Youth Empowerment Day</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>09:00 AM:</strong> Inter-school cultural quizzes and debates, and an essay competition focused on Ngemba history and language preservation by NSU National President.</li>
          <li><strong>03:00 PM:</strong> Handover of school supplies, academic scholarships, and prizes by the NDECA Education Committee.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Tuesday December 15th — Mbieg’ndoung (Day 5)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Health Wellness Drive</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>08:00 AM:</strong> Commencement of free medical screening campaign at the Nsongwa Palace (consultations, eye tests, blood pressure, diabetic screening, etc.), coordinated by the Mary Alieh Foundation.</li>
          <li><strong>10:00 AM:</strong> Public health sensitization seminar on preventive medicine, hygiene, and clean potable water by the Bamenda Regional Hospital in partnership with the Mary Alieh Foundation.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Wednesday December 16th — Yinkoung (Day 6)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Sports, Health & Traditional Wrestling</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>08:00 AM:</strong> Conclude the free medical screening and distribute prescribed medications.</li>
          <li><strong>10:00 AM:</strong> Traditional wrestling matches, tug of war (between youths of neighboring quarters) Quarter Heads to arrange.</li>
          <li><strong>02:00 PM:</strong> KICK-OFF, Fo’o Ngwadeza III Silver Jubilee Football Tournament (Semi-Finals Matches)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Thursday December 17th — San’neh (Day 7)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Women Empowerment & Culinary Arts Day</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>09:00 AM:</strong> General Assembly of all Nsongwa Women’s Cultural groups, Mothers’ Union, Dance Groups, Age groups (Nkang), etc.</li>
          <li><strong>11:00 AM:</strong> Traditional culinary competition: Live exhibition of authentic NGEUMBA dishes (Achu, yellow soup, black soup, Akwa, etc.).</li>
          <li><strong>02:00 PM:</strong> Seminar on micro-trade, financial literacy, and Cooperative/Bank management, hosted by Credit Unions and Banks.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Friday December 18th — Mbig’neh (Day 8)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Arts, Craft & Museum Launching</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>09:00 AM:</strong> Exhibition of Nsongwa traditional wood carvings, Royal garments, pottery and beadwork.</li>
          <li><strong>11:30 AM:</strong> Symposium: “Preserving the Nsongwa-Ngemba identity in a Digital World.”</li>
          <li><strong>02:00 PM:</strong> NEUKWI RITES</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Saturday December 19th — Yinkaheh (Day 9)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Diaspora Homecoming & Welcoming Rites</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>10:00 AM:</strong> Arrival and traditional welcoming ceremony for Nsongwa elites returning from the USA, Europe, South Africa, the UAE, and national cities (Douala, Fako, Yaounde, Bafoussam, Limbe, Kumba, and others).</li>
          <li><strong>01:00 PM:</strong> Interactive town hall session: Diaspora investment for infrastructure and sustainable Development in Nsongwa.</li>
          <li><strong>07:00 PM:</strong> Traditional night: Evening reception and dinner hosted by the Palace for all home-comers.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Sunday December 20th — Mametah (Day 10)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Sports Finals & Corporate Activation Day</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>10:00 AM:</strong> Corporate exhibition hours: Direct Customer Service, activation, and promotion by headline partners (MTN Cameroon, United Bank of Africa (UBA), ORANGE Cameroun, ECOBANK, Union Camerounaise des Brasseries (UCB), Boissons du Cameroun SA, CAMTEL, Union Bank of Cameroon (UBC), CREDIT UNIONS, and Others).</li>
          <li><strong>03:00 PM:</strong> Grand Finale of the Fo’o Ngwadeza III Silver Jubilee Football Tournament</li>
          <li><strong>05:30 PM:</strong> Trophy presentation and corporate networking evening.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Monday December 21st — Yidzong (Day 11)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">General Assembly & Developmental Blueprint</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>09:00 AM:</strong> NDECA Annual General Assembly: Review of community achievements, assessments, and evaluation of Infrastructure Development Projects.</li>
          <li><strong>12:00 AM:</strong> Traditional Decorations/Recognitions.</li>
          <li><strong>01:00 PM:</strong> Launch of Nsongwa 2027/2028 Vision (FOCUSING ON CLEAN WATER, EXPANSION OF ELECTRICITY, ROAD NETWORKS, ETC).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Tuesday December 22nd — Yakab (Day 12)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">End of Neukwi - Convocation of Dignitaries - Traditional Rulers, Administrative Authorities</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>10:00 AM:</strong> Official arrival, reception, and traditional protocol welcoming of visiting Fons from across the Northwest and other parts of the country.</li>
          <li><strong>10:30 AM:</strong> Arrival of Administrative Officials</li>
          <li><strong>11:00 AM:</strong> Royal solidarity parade and fraternal cultural exchanges between visiting traditional delegations.</li>
          <li><strong>1:00 PM:</strong> Private inner-palace royal banquet for visiting Fons and Administrative Officials.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
